# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/chains_minor.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event forbidden_annotations
# en: Three Colours of Ink
title [287aa3] = 三色墨水
# en: You read Odile's notebook properly at last, at a desk within sight of the locked door. Black ink for the shelves, green for the prefects' rounds, red for warnings. Half the red is underlined twice.
text [b5e905] = 你终于认真读起了奥迪尔的笔记本，就坐在能望见那扇锁着的门的书桌前。黑墨水记书架，绿墨水记级长巡逻，红墨水记警告。一半的红字下面画了两道线。
# en: A battered notebook open on a library desk, its margins crowded with notes in red, green and black ink, a silver key lying across the page.
scene [904394] = 图书馆书桌上摊开一本破旧的笔记本，页边挤满红、绿、黑三色批注，一把银钥匙横放在书页上。
# en: Learn the prefects' rounds
opt.left.label [be7ef0] = 记下级长的巡逻
# en: Easier to slip in unseen.
opt.left.hint [fd6b1e] = 更容易悄悄溜进去。
# en: Green ink: the prefect on library duty walks the east stacks at nine and the west at ten, and stops for tea in between. You learn it like a timetable.
opt.left.say.1 [e877ee] = 绿墨水写着：图书馆值班的级长九点巡东边书架，十点巡西边，中间要喝一杯茶。你像背课表一样把它背了下来。
# en: Learn the shelf marks
opt.right.label [9e4e50] = 记下书架标记
# en: Know what not to touch.
opt.right.hint [d93e85] = 知道什么不能碰。
# en: Black ink and red: which shelves are safe, which books are bound in something that isn't leather, and, underlined twice, "never with bare hands".
opt.right.say.1 [06490c] = 黑墨水和红墨水写着：哪些书架是安全的，哪些书的封皮不是皮革，还有一句画了两道线的——“千万别用手直接碰”。

@event forbidden_section_1
# en: The Silver Key
title [f6e05e] = 银钥匙
# en: After hours. The silver key fits the Restricted Section door perfectly. Beyond it, shelves of black-bound books breathe softly in the dark. Somewhere, a prefect's footsteps.
text [190679] = 过了闭馆时间。银钥匙严丝合缝地插进了禁书区的门锁。门后，一排排黑皮书在黑暗中轻轻呼吸。不知哪里，传来级长的脚步声。
# en: A heavy iron door at the end of a library aisle, a silver key turning in its lock, a candle held low.
scene [f9b84e] = 图书馆过道尽头一扇沉重的铁门，一把银钥匙在锁孔里转动，一支蜡烛压得很低。
# en: Turn back
opt.left.label [2f9f2d] = 回头
# en: You lock the door again and hang the key on a nail in your wardrobe. Some nights you hear it rattling.
opt.left.say.1 [9742c9] = 你把门重新锁好，把钥匙挂在衣柜里的钉子上。有些夜里，你能听见它在哗啦作响。
# en: Slip inside
opt.right.label [316541] = 溜进去
# en: You spend two hours reading by candle-stub. You leave with a head full of things no student should know, and the certainty that you'll come back.
opt.right.say.1 [ed65bb] = 你借着蜡烛头读了两个小时。离开时，脑子里装满了任何学生都不该知道的东西，也确信自己还会再来。
# en: Bram Hollis is waiting by the door when you come out. He is smiling. It's the worst smile you've ever seen.
opt.right.say.2 [84c17d] = 你出来时，布拉姆·霍利斯正等在门边。他在笑。那是你见过最糟糕的笑容。

@event forbidden_bram_watch
# en: The Prefect at the Door
title [056c09] = 门口的级长
# en: {Bram Hollis is leaning on the Restricted Section door, lantern at his feet, as if he has all night. Somebody has told him about the key, or he has guessed.|Bram is at the door again. He has brought a sandwich this time.|Bram's watch on the door has become a habit. He hums while he waits, badly.}
text [c78094] = {布拉姆·霍利斯靠在禁书区的门上，提灯放在脚边，好像有一整夜的时间。有人跟他说了钥匙的事，要不就是他猜到了。|布拉姆又守在门口。这回他还带了个三明治。|布拉姆守门已经成了习惯。他一边等一边哼歌，哼得很难听。}
# en: A broad prefect leaning against an iron library door with folded arms, a lantern at his feet, a student watching from behind a bookcase.
scene [6c3388] = 一个身材魁梧的级长抱着胳膊靠在图书馆的铁门上，提灯放在脚边，一个学生躲在书架后面偷看。
# en: Wait him out in the stacks
opt.left.label [33dbcb] = 躲在书架间等他走
# en: Cold and cramped, but unseen.
opt.left.hint [b9f103] = 又冷又挤，但不会被发现。
# en: {You crouch behind the history shelves for an hour, reading by the light of his lantern, until he gives up and goes to bed.|You wait him out, and he eats the whole sandwich first. Your knees will never forgive you.|You know his humming now. When it stops, he's asleep on his feet, and you slip past.}
opt.left.say.1 [176864] = {你蹲在历史书架后面一个小时，借着他的提灯光看书，直到他放弃回去睡觉。|你等他走，可他先把整个三明治吃完了。你的膝盖永远不会原谅你。|你现在听得出他的哼歌了。歌声一停，他就站着睡着了，你从他身边溜了过去。}
# en: Bluff your way past
opt.right.label [24be4a] = 骗过他
# en: Guile against a prefect who wants to catch you.
opt.right.hint [8e22c2] = 用诡术对付一个一心想抓你的级长。
# en: {You tell him a professor is looking for him in the east tower. He goes. You are inside before his lantern reaches the stair.|"Thorne wants you," you say, and Bram's face goes pale. Nobody checks whether Thorne wants them.|You tell him there's a fight in the courtyard. There isn't. He's gone before you finish the sentence.}
opt.right.say.1 [bd8b7f] = {你告诉他有位教授在东塔找他。他走了。他的提灯还没到楼梯口，你已经进去了。|“索恩教授找你。”你说，布拉姆的脸一下子白了。没人会去核实索恩教授是不是真在找自己。|你告诉他院子里有人打架。根本没有。你话还没说完他就跑了。}
# en: {"Nice try," says Bram, and writes your name in his little book with great pleasure.|He laughs, actually laughs, and walks you back to your dormitory by the ear.|Bram has heard that one before, from you. He takes your name, and his time over it.}
opt.right.say.2 [779b9f] = {“想得美。”布拉姆说，兴高采烈地把你的名字记进他的小本子。|他笑了，真的笑出了声，然后揪着你的耳朵把你送回了宿舍。|这套说辞布拉姆已经从你嘴里听过一次了。他记下你的名字，慢条斯理，不慌不忙。}

@event forbidden_section_2
# en: The Codex of Hollow Names
title [b71797] = 《空洞名录》
# en: You keep going back. One night, a book finds you. It falls from a high shelf and lands open at your feet: the Codex of Hollow Names. The first page is a list of names. The last one is still being written. It's yours.{flag(forbidden_warned):  Odile's warning comes back to you: don't let a book choose you.|}
text [64e882] = 你一次又一次地回去。某天夜里，一本书找上了你。它从高高的书架上掉下来，摊开落在你脚边：《空洞名录》。第一页是一串名字。最后一个名字还在书写中。是你的名字。{flag(forbidden_warned): 奥迪尔的警告浮上心头：别让一本书选中你。|}
# en: A book bound in something that is not leather, open on a reading stand, its letters slowly rearranging themselves.
scene [a07d02] = 一本用某种不是皮革的东西装订的书摊在阅读架上，字母正缓缓重新排列。
# en: Put it back
opt.left.label [862ed2] = 把它放回去
# en: You shelve it. When you look back, it has fallen again, open at the same page.
opt.left.say.1 [5dc723] = 你把它放回书架。回头一看，它又掉了下来，摊开在同一页。
# en: Read it
opt.right.label [fb8482] = 读它
# en: You read until dawn. You learn about the thing under the lake. When you finally close the book, your fingertips are grey.
opt.right.say.1 [f6835c] = 你一直读到天亮。你了解了湖底的那个东西。终于合上书时，你的指尖变成了灰色。
# en: You read until dawn and close the book with shaking hands. Some things you can't unread.
opt.right.say.2 [c47a6e] = 你一直读到天亮，用颤抖的手合上了书。有些东西，读过就再也忘不掉。

@event forbidden_fourth_year
# en: Odile's Last Week
title [e07520] = 奥迪尔的最后一周
# en: Odile Varn finds you between the stacks with her satchel already packed. She leaves at the end of term. "You used the key," she says. It isn't a question. "I won't ask what you found. Unless you want to tell me."
text [67d7ff] = 奥迪尔·瓦恩在书架间找到你，书包已经收拾好了。她这学期结束就走。“你用过钥匙了。”她说。这不是问句。“我不问你发现了什么。除非你想告诉我。”
# en: A fourth-year with a packed satchel leaning on a library shelf, talking quietly to a younger student between the stacks.
scene [91edf1] = 一个背着收拾好的书包的四年级生靠在图书馆书架上，在书架间低声和一个年轻学生说话。
# en: Tell her what you've seen
opt.left.label [d36021] = 告诉她你看到的
# en: She has a warning for you.
opt.left.hint [a01664] = 她有一句警告给你。
# en: She listens to all of it, then puts a hand on your notebook. "Some books want readers," she says. "If one falls open at your feet, don't let it choose you." Then she hugs you, briefly, and is gone.
opt.left.say.1 [05ed28] = 她听完了一切，然后把手按在你的笔记本上。“有些书想要读者，”她说，“要是有一本摊开落在你脚边，别让它选中你。”然后她匆匆抱了你一下，走了。
# en: Keep it to yourself
opt.right.label [09de43] = 守口如瓶
# en: Your secret stays yours.
opt.right.hint [9d2616] = 你的秘密只属于你。
# en: She smiles, as if that were the right answer. "Good," she says. "That's how I kept it too." She leaves you her spare candle-stubs and a list of the quietest desks.
opt.right.say.1 [2312ee] = 她笑了，好像这才是正确答案。“很好，”她说，“我当年也是这么守着的。”她把剩下的蜡烛头和一张最安静书桌的清单留给了你。

@event forbidden_section_3
# en: Caught
title [63a445] = 被抓了
# en: A lantern blazes in the doorway. Not a prefect this time: the headmistress herself. She looks at the book in your hands, then at you, for a very long time. "Most students who find that book," she says, "don't put it down."
text [cff27d] = 门口亮起一盏灯笼。这次不是级长：是院长本人。她看了看你手里的书，又看了看你，看了很久很久。“大多数找到那本书的学生，”她说，“都放不下它。”
# en: A tall silhouette in the doorway of the Restricted Section, holding a lantern that casts long shadows over a startled student.
scene [21af3f] = 禁书区门口一个高大的剪影，手中提灯在受惊的学生身上投下长长的影子。
# en: Apologise and accept punishment
opt.left.label [17d414] = 道歉，接受惩罚
# en: She takes the key. "Detention, every evening this month; your coursework can wait. And come to my tower on Thursdays. If you're going to learn dangerous things, you'll learn them properly."
opt.left.say.1 [19d763] = 她收走了钥匙。“禁闭，这个月每天晚上；你的功课只能先放一放。还有，每周四到我的塔楼来。既然你要学危险的东西，就该学得像样。”
# en: Ask her what it means
opt.right.label [a565a0] = 问她这意味着什么
# en: A long pause. "It means something is waking, and it is looking for help. Make sure it doesn't find yours." She takes the key, leaves you the candle, and forgets, or chooses to forget, the detention.
opt.right.say.1 [c0f71e] = 长久的沉默。“意味着有东西在苏醒，而且它在寻找帮手。别让它找到你的帮助。”她拿走了钥匙，把蜡烛留给了你，也忘了——或者说故意忘了——禁闭的事。

@event curse_cure_1
# en: A Cold That Won't Leave
title [a74f1f] = 驱不散的寒意
# en: {&The cold under your skin is getting worse.|The cold is back, worse than before.} Sister Amaranth's tonics do nothing. She looks troubled. "This isn't an illness. It's a hunger." She lowers her voice. "Old Maud might know something. Don't tell anyone I said so."
text [fd21ec] = {&皮肤下的寒意越来越重了。|寒意又回来了，比上次更重。}阿玛兰斯修女的药剂毫无作用。她面露忧色。“这不是病。是一种饥饿。”她压低声音，“老莫德也许知道些什么。别说是我说的。”
# en: A student wrapped in three blankets beside a roaring fire, breath still fogging the air, fingertips grey.
scene [ecf450] = 一个学生裹着三层毯子坐在熊熊炉火旁，呼出的气仍凝成白雾，指尖发灰。
# en: Endure it
opt.left.label [9e8205] = 忍着
# en: You pile on blankets and keep going. The cold whispers sometimes. You pretend not to hear. Maud, you suppose, will still be there if it gets worse.
opt.left.say.1 [10575f] = 你堆上毯子，继续过日子。寒意有时会低语。你假装没听见。你想，要是更糟了，莫德总还在那儿。
# en: Go to Old Maud
opt.right.label [fb88bc] = 去找老莫德
# en: Maud takes one look at your fingertips and puts the kettle on. "Moonpetal," she says. "Grows in the Whisperwood. Only blooms after dark. You'll fetch it yourself — the cure has to come from the cursed."
opt.right.say.1 [aa1b58] = 莫德看了一眼你的指尖，就把水壶放上了炉子。“月瓣花，”她说，“长在低语森林里。只在天黑后开。你得自己去采——解药必须来自被诅咒的人。”

@event curse_cure_2
# en: Moonpetal
title [676f04] = 月瓣花
# en: The Whisperwood after dark. Things move between the trees. In a clearing, a single silver flower is opening, and between you and it stands a stag made of shadow.
text [b47cd6] = 天黑后的低语森林。树林间有东西在移动。一片空地上，一朵银色的花正在绽放，而你和它之间，站着一头由阴影构成的雄鹿。
# en: A dark forest at nightfall, a single silver flower glowing in a clearing, eyes watching from between the trees.
scene [4d6ecf] = 暮色中漆黑的森林，空地上一朵银花发着光，树影间有眼睛在窥视。
# en: Sneak around it
opt.left.label [efbf19] = 绕过它
# en: You creep through the bracken and pluck the moonpetal. Maud's brew tastes like moonlight and burnt sugar. The cold is gone.
opt.left.say.1 [1fb52a] = 你悄悄穿过蕨丛，摘下了月瓣花。莫德熬的药尝起来像月光和焦糖。寒意消失了。
# en: The stag sees you. You run. No moonpetal tonight; you'll have to come back.
opt.left.say.2 [f03c88] = 雄鹿看见了你。你拔腿就跑。今晚没有月瓣花了；你得再来一趟。
# en: Face the stag
opt.right.label [c629ba] = 直面雄鹿
# en: You stand your ground. The stag lowers its head — and steps aside. Maud's brew drives the cold out of your bones.
opt.right.say.1 [eecd0a] = 你站定不动。雄鹿低下头——然后让开了路。莫德的药把寒意从你骨子里驱了出去。
# en: The stag charges. You wake up in the bracken at dawn. Maud bandages you. "Another night," she says.
opt.right.say.2 [056977] = 雄鹿冲了过来。黎明时你在蕨丛里醒来。莫德给你包扎。“改天晚上再来。”她说。

@event grisk_offer
# en: A Helpful Goblin
title [6c54bd] = 乐于助人的地精
# en: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat falls into step beside you. "Grisk," he says, "friend to the temporarily embarrassed. Sixty crowns, today. Twelve a month for six months. Very reasonable."
text [266d6d] = 一个穿天鹅绒马甲的地精走到你身边，和你并肩同行。“格里斯克，”他说，“暂时手头紧的人的朋友。今天给你六十克朗。每月还十二，还六个月。非常合理。”
# en: A small goblin in a velvet waistcoat and pince-nez, sitting on a crate in an alley, a ledger in one hand and a quill behind his ear.
scene [a36b2a] = 一个穿天鹅绒马甲、戴夹鼻眼镜的小地精坐在小巷的木箱上，一手拿着账簿，耳后夹着羽毛笔。
# en: No thank you
opt.left.label [6c52d1] = 不用了，谢谢
# en: "My door is always open," Grisk says. You suspect it is actually always locked.
opt.left.say.1 [1a3e29] = “我的门永远为你敞开。”格里斯克说。你怀疑它其实永远锁着。
# en: Take the loan
opt.right.label [e30491] = 接受贷款
# en: He counts out sixty crowns, writes your name in the ledger and smiles with a great many teeth.
opt.right.say.1 [35d10d] = 他数出六十克朗，把你的名字写进账簿，笑着露出了非常多的牙齿。

@event grisk_board_debt
# en: Settled, With Interest
title [3033c4] = 已结清，外加利息
# en: The bursar's office has stopped sending reminders. Instead, Grisk is waiting outside it with a receipt. "Two months' board, paid in full," he beams. "By me. A loan, naturally, with a little extra for your pocket. Twelve a month for six months. You can sign here."
text [72d609] = 财务处已经不再寄催缴单了。取而代之的是，格里斯克拿着一张收据等在门外。“两个月的伙食费，全额付清，”他笑容满面，“我付的。当然是借款，外加一点零花钱。每月十二，还六个月。在这儿签字就行。”
# en: A goblin in a velvet waistcoat waiting outside the bursar's office, waving a receipt like a small flag.
scene [c90a78] = 一个穿天鹅绒马甲的地精等在财务处门外，像挥小旗一样挥着一张收据。
# en: Sign his ledger
opt.left.label [d542c5] = 在他的账本上签字
# en: You sign. He has already paid the board out of it; he counts the rest into your palm and writes your name in the ledger with a flourish that has teeth in it.
opt.left.say.1 [28c617] = 你签了字。伙食费他已经从里头付掉了；剩下的他数进你的掌心，在账本上龙飞凤舞地写下你的名字——那一笔带着獠牙。
# en: Beg the bursar for time
opt.right.label [ba6715] = 去求财务处宽限
# en: You spend an afternoon on a hard bench outside the bursar's office and leave with a month's grace and the feeling of having been looked at over spectacles for a very long time.
opt.right.say.1 [1267b3] = 你在财务处门外的硬板凳上坐了一下午，最后换来一个月的宽限，以及被人从眼镜上方久久打量的感觉。

@event grisk_favour
# en: Grisk's Proposition
title [5cdd5b] = 格里斯克的提议
# en: Grisk finds you in the library. "I could cancel your debt," he murmurs. "A small favour. There's a book in the archive — the Founders' Ledger. A client wants a page. Just one page."
text [816cbf] = 格里斯克在图书馆找到了你。“我可以免了你的债，”他低声说，“帮个小忙就行。档案库里有本书——《创始者账簿》。有位客户想要其中一页。就一页。”
# en: The goblin moneylender leaning close in a library alcove, pushing a slip of paper across a table.
scene [64ffac] = 地精放贷人在图书馆的壁龛里凑近，把一张纸条推过桌面。
# en: Refuse
opt.left.label [cada35] = 拒绝
# en: "Pity." He makes a note in his ledger. It looks expensive.
opt.left.say.1 [84fdf0] = “可惜。”他在账簿上记了一笔。看起来代价不小。
# en: Do the favour
opt.right.label [c95c1c] = 帮这个忙
# en: You razor a page from the oldest ledger in the archive. Grisk tears up your debt. You notice the page had a black star on it.
opt.right.say.1 [3798eb] = 你从档案库最古老的账簿上割下了一页。格里斯克撕掉了你的欠条。你注意到那一页上有一颗黑星。
# en: The archivist catches you with a razor in your hand. Detention. Grisk is nowhere to be found, and the debt stands.
opt.right.say.2 [17b625] = 档案管理员撞见你手里拿着刀片。禁闭。格里斯克不见踪影，债务照旧。

@event grisk_smuggling
# en: One More Job
title [5823eb] = 再干一票
# en: Grisk again. "You were so good last time. I have parcels that need carrying: collected at the boathouse at midnight, delivered to the village by day. Thirty crowns a parcel. Steady work, for steady hands."
text [e0fb8b] = 又是格里斯克。“上次你干得真漂亮。我有些包裹需要人送：午夜在船屋取货，白天送到村里。一个包裹三十克朗。稳定的活儿，给手稳的人。”
# en: A crate of clinking bottles hidden under a tarp on a dark boathouse dock, a small goblin silhouetted against the lake.
scene [539e69] = 漆黑的船屋码头上，一只装满叮当作响的瓶子的箱子藏在油布下，湖面映出一个小地精的剪影。
# en: You're done with him
opt.left.label [71da7e] = 你和他到此为止了
# en: "Everyone's done with me eventually," Grisk says, without rancour. You never see him again.
opt.left.say.1 [288fa5] = “大家最后都会跟我到此为止的。”格里斯克毫无怨气地说。你再也没见过他。
# en: Hear him out
opt.right.label [b1225b] = 听他说下去
# en: He explains the arrangement: the jetty, midnight, oilcloth, a cobbler's back door. "Any month you like," he says. "I'm very flexible." You walk away with the arrangement in your head, and it won't leave.
opt.right.say.1 [69c60d] = 他把安排讲给你听：码头，午夜，油布包，鞋匠铺的后门。“哪个月都行，”他说，“我很好商量。”你走开时，这套安排一直在你脑子里转，赶也赶不走。

@event fox_injured
# en: Smoke in the Woods
title [bf8cb4] = 林间青烟
# en: At the edge of the forest, a thin plume of smoke. A small fox is caught in a rusted snare, its tail smouldering like an ember. It snarls at you, then whimpers.
text [b3132b] = 森林边缘，升起一缕细细的烟。一只小狐狸被生锈的捕兽夹夹住了，尾巴像余烬一样冒着火星。它冲你龇牙，然后呜咽起来。
# en: A small red fox lying in the snow at the forest edge, its tail smouldering like a dying campfire, one paw caught in a rusted snare.
scene [b579d6] = 森林边缘的雪地里躺着一只小红狐，尾巴像将熄的篝火般闷燃，一只爪子卡在生锈的捕兽夹里。
# en: Leave it — it's wild
opt.left.label [d9cfe4] = 别管——它是野的
# en: You walk away. That night you dream of smoke.
opt.left.say.1 [6bc432] = 你走开了。那天夜里，你梦见了烟。
# en: Free it and bandage the paw
opt.right.label [8a0394] = 放了它，包扎爪子
# en: It bites you, of course. But it lets you wrap the paw. Then it limps into the trees, glancing back once with eyes like embers.
opt.right.say.1 [113ea7] = 它当然咬了你一口。但它让你把爪子包扎好了。然后它一瘸一拐地走进树林，回头看了你一眼，眼睛像余烬。

@event fox_returns
# en: A Visitor at the Window
title [8da400] = 窗边的访客
# en: Two months later, a fox with a glowing tail is sitting on your windowsill. Its paw has healed. At its feet: a small, dusty ruby.
text [635017] = 两个月后，一只尾巴发光的狐狸坐在你的窗台上。它的爪子已经好了。它脚边放着一颗小小的、蒙尘的红宝石。
# en: A fox with a softly glowing tail sitting on a stone windowsill at dawn, a ruby glinting at its feet.
scene [41ab76] = 黎明时分，一只尾巴柔柔发光的狐狸坐在石砌窗台上，脚边闪着一颗红宝石。
# en: Shoo it away
opt.left.label [01018d] = 把它赶走
# en: It leaves the ruby and vanishes. You sell the ruby. Somehow you feel you've failed a test.
opt.left.say.1 [4959d7] = 它留下红宝石就消失了。你卖掉了红宝石。不知为何，你觉得自己没通过某种考验。
# en: Open the window
opt.right.label [15dfe6] = 打开窗户
# en: It hops in, inspects your room thoroughly and falls asleep on your pillow. Your pillow is now slightly scorched. You don't mind.
opt.right.say.1 [d3c253] = 它跳进来，把你的房间仔仔细细检查了一遍，然后在你的枕头上睡着了。你的枕头现在有点焦了。你不介意。

@event fox_bond
# en: Ember
title [c95de4] = 余烬
# en: The fox has decided. {term: It follows you to class|It follows you through the half-empty corridors}, sleeps on your feet and growls at Bram. Students aren't allowed unregistered familiars. Registering one costs fifteen crowns.
text [ccfb40] = 狐狸已经做了决定。{term: 它跟着你去上课|它跟着你穿过半空的走廊}，睡在你脚上，还冲布拉姆低吼。学生不允许拥有未登记的魔宠。登记一只要十五克朗。
# en: A student and a small fire-tailed fox nose to nose, a soft golden light connecting them.
scene [f6fbd2] = 一个学生和一只火尾小狐狸鼻尖相对，一道柔和的金光把他们连在一起。
# en: Hide her
opt.left.label [ce99de] = 把她藏起来
# en: You name her Ember. Nobody notices a fox that doesn't want to be noticed.
opt.left.say.1 [9f2aee] = 你给她取名“余烬”。一只不想被注意的狐狸，没人会注意到。
# en: A professor spots her at once. You pay what you can of the fee — and Ember is yours, officially.
opt.left.say.2 [8afb09] = 一位教授一眼就发现了她。你尽力交了能交的费用——余烬正式成了你的魔宠。
# en: Register her properly
opt.right.label [9506c8] = 正式登记
# en: The registrar stamps a form. "Name?" "Ember," you say. The fox looks smug.
opt.right.say.1 [c579b1] = 登记员在表格上盖了章。“名字？”“余烬。”你说。狐狸一脸得意。

@event fox_helps
# en: Ember Finds Something
title [020478] = 余烬找到了东西
# en: {~Ember drags you, by the sleeve, through three corridors and a hedge. She's found something. She's very proud of it.|Ember sits on your book until you look at her. She has found something, and she has buried it, and now she wants you to dig.|Ember comes back from the lake with her tail steaming and something in her jaws. She drops it at your feet like a gift.}
text [1b03f8] = {~余烬叼着你的袖子，拖你穿过三条走廊和一道树篱。她找到了东西。她非常骄傲。|余烬坐在你的书上，直到你看向她。她找到了东西，还把它埋了起来，现在要你去挖。|余烬从湖边回来，尾巴冒着热气，嘴里叼着什么。她把它放在你脚边，像献上一份礼物。}
# en: A fox nosing through dry leaves under a hedge and emerging with a purse in its jaws.
scene [fa286c] = 一只狐狸在树篱下的枯叶里拱来拱去，叼出一只钱袋。
# en: Let her keep it
opt.left.label [dacce7] = 让她留着吧
# en: {~It's a sock. Ember is thrilled. You are thrilled for her.|It's a glove that smells of the stables. Ember sleeps on it for a week.|It's a pine cone, slightly charred. She guards it from Bram personally.}
opt.left.say.1 [0fa900] = {~是一只袜子。余烬高兴坏了。你也替她高兴。|是一只带着马厩味的手套。余烬在上面睡了一个星期。|是一颗烧焦了一点的松果。她亲自看着它，不让布拉姆靠近。}
# en: See what it is
opt.right.label [c3d611] = 看看是什么
# en: A lost purse. You return it to its owner, who insists you keep the reward.
opt.right.say.1 [8c1c68] = 一只丢失的钱袋。你把它还给了失主，失主坚持要你收下酬谢。
# en: A lost page from a professor's lecture notes. Enlightening.
opt.right.say.2 [3f4db6] = 一页遗失的教授讲义。很有启发。

@event ghost_socks
# en: Rearranged Socks
title [c1194d] = 被整理的袜子
# en: Every morning, your socks have been rearranged. By colour. Then alphabetically by colour. Last night they spelled out "HELP".
text [79fec3] = 每天早上，你的袜子都被重新整理过。按颜色。然后按颜色的首字母排序。昨晚，它们拼出了“救命”。
# en: A dormitory drawer open in candlelight, socks arranged in a careful spiral, a faint shimmer in the air above them.
scene [c7a0d1] = 烛光中一只打开的宿舍抽屉，袜子被整齐地排成螺旋，上方的空气里有一丝微光。
# en: Ignore it
opt.left.label [e2ae0c] = 不去管它
# en: You buy new socks. The next morning they're arranged by mood.
opt.left.say.1 [57e0f1] = 你买了新袜子。第二天早上，它们按心情排好了。
# en: Stay up and watch
opt.right.label [03406b] = 熬夜守着
# en: At three in the morning, the drawer slides open by itself.
opt.right.say.1 [69a0e4] = 凌晨三点，抽屉自己滑开了。

@event ghost_reveal
# en: Prudence
title [a6d175] = 普鲁登丝
# en: A girl in old-fashioned robes, translucent and very polite. "Prudence Ashworth, class of 1793. Terribly sorry about the socks. I never finished my letter. Could you deliver it? The village. The bakery. Please."
text [fd675e] = 一个穿着老式长袍的女孩，半透明，非常有礼貌。“普鲁登丝·阿什沃斯，1793 届。袜子的事实在抱歉。我的信一直没写完。你能帮我送去吗？镇上。面包店。拜托了。”
# en: A translucent girl in old-fashioned school robes, hovering by a window, holding a faded letter.
scene [2de1ba] = 一个身穿老式校袍的半透明女孩悬浮在窗边，手里拿着一封褪色的信。
# en: Exorcise her
opt.left.label [eb2bc2] = 驱散她
# en: You speak the banishing rite. She fades with a small, hurt look. Your socks stay put after that. You feel a bit rotten.
opt.left.say.1 [940567] = 你念出驱逐仪式的咒文。她带着一点受伤的神情消散了。从那以后你的袜子再没动过。你觉得自己有点混蛋。
# en: Promise to deliver it
opt.right.label [32f8b3] = 答应帮她送信
# en: She claps her translucent hands. "Oh, thank you! It's only taken two hundred years."
opt.right.say.1 [e468ed] = 她拍着半透明的双手。“噢，谢谢你！才等了两百年而已。”

@event ghost_letter
# en: A Letter Two Hundred Years Late
title [4de394] = 迟到两百年的信
# en: The bakery has been in the same family for two hundred years. The old baker reads Prudence's letter at the counter. "My great-great-great-grandmother waited for this," she says. "She never stopped."
text [07ef08] = 这家面包店两百年来一直由同一个家族经营。老面包师在柜台前读着普鲁登丝的信。“我的高高高祖母一直在等这封信，”她说，“她从没停止过等待。”
# en: A cosy village bakery, an old baker reading a yellowed letter with tears on her cheeks, a ghostly figure smiling in the doorway.
scene [481d5e] = 温馨的小镇面包店，一位老面包师读着一封泛黄的信，泪流满面，门口一个幽灵般的身影在微笑。
# en: Stay and listen to the story
opt.left.label [7f246b] = 留下来听这个故事
# en: Prudence was in love with the baker's daughter. When you return, the ghost is waiting, glowing like a sunrise. Then she's gone, at peace.
opt.left.say.1 [623354] = 原来普鲁登丝爱着面包师的女儿。你回去时，幽灵正等着你，像日出一样发着光。然后她走了，安详地。
# en: Leave quietly
opt.right.label [69ae5f] = 悄悄离开
# en: The baker presses a free loaf into your hands. That night, your socks are arranged into a heart. Then never again.
opt.right.say.1 [104d89] = 面包师把一条面包塞进你手里，不收钱。那天夜里，你的袜子被摆成了一颗心。之后再也没有过。
